    "excerpt": [
      {
        "line": 2710,
        "text": "not an improvement theorem from the Younis paper."
      },
      {
        "line": 2711,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 2712,
        "text": "\\begin{proposition}[A centered KDM density-score control]"
      },
      {
        "line": 2713,
        "text": "\\label{prop:kdm-density-control}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2714,
        "text": "Condition on a pilot mixture with fixed positive weights $\\pi_j$ summing"
      },
      {
        "line": 2715,
        "text": "to one, means $\\mu_j$, and positive definite covariances $B_j$. Define"
      },
      {
        "line": 2716,
        "text": "\\begin{equation}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2717,
        "text": " m_{a,s}(z)=\\sum_{j=1}^M\\pi_j"
      },
      {
        "line": 2718,
        "text": "   \\mathcal N(z;\\mu_j+a,e^{2s}B_j),\\qquad"
      },
      {
        "line": 2719,
        "text": " C(z)=\\left.\\nabla_{(a,s)}\\log m_{a,s}(z)\\right|_{a=0,s=0}."
      },
      {
        "line": 2720,
        "text": " \\label{eq:kdm-density-control}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2721,
        "text": "\\end{equation}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2722,
        "text": "For $Z\\sim m_{0,0}$, $\\mathbb E[C(Z)\\mid\\text{pilot}]=0$."
      },
      {
        "line": 2723,
        "text": "Let a baseline vector score $G$ use any coupling with $Z$ that preserves"
      },
      {
        "line": 2724,
        "text": "these marginals. If a coefficient matrix $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is fixed, or fitted on"
      },
      {
        "line": 2725,
        "text": "calibration randomness independent of the evaluation randomness conditional"
      },
      {
        "line": 2726,
        "text": "on the pilot, then"
      },
      {
        "line": 2727,
        "text": "\\begin{equation}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2728,
        "text": " \\mathbb E[G-\\boldsymbol{\\beta} C(Z)\\mid\\text{pilot,calibration}]"
      },
      {
        "line": 2729,
        "text": " =\\mathbb E[G\\mid\\text{pilot,calibration}]."
      },
      {
        "line": 2730,
        "text": "\\end{equation}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2731,
        "text": "Assume the required second moments exist when comparing variances."
      },
      {
        "line": 2732,
        "text": "\\end{proposition}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2733,
        "text": "\\begin{proof}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2734,
        "text": "Differentiating the normalized finite Gaussian mixture under its integral"
      },
      {
        "line": 2735,
        "text": "is valid for translation and scale in a neighborhood of the fixed positive"
      },
      {
        "line": 2736,
        "text": "definite covariances. Thus"
      },
      {
        "line": 2737,
        "text": "\\["
      },
      {
        "line": 2738,
        "text": " \\mathbb E C(Z)=\\int m_{0,0}(z)"
      },
      {
        "line": 2739,
        "text": "  \\frac{\\left.\\nabla_{(a,s)}m_{a,s}(z)\\right|_{0,0}}{m_{0,0}(z)}\\,\\dd z"
      },
      {
        "line": 2740,
        "text": "  =\\left.\\nabla_{(a,s)}\\int m_{a,s}(z)\\,\\dd z\\right|_{0,0}=0."
      },
      {
        "line": 2741,
        "text": "\\]"
      },
      {
        "line": 2742,
        "text": "Conditioning on the independent pilot and calibration makes $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ fixed"
      },
      {
        "line": 2743,
        "text": "and leaves the evaluation mixture law unchanged. Linearity of conditional"
      },
      {
        "line": 2744,
        "text": "expectation gives the second assertion."
      },
      {
        "line": 2745,
        "text": "\\end{proof}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2746,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 2747,
        "text": "Writing $r_j(z)$ for the mixture responsibilities, the translation control"
      },
      {
        "line": 2748,
        "text": "is $\\sum_j r_j(z)B_j^{-1}(z-\\mu_j)$, and the scale control is"
      },
      {
        "line": 2749,
        "text": "$\\sum_jr_j(z)\\{(z-\\mu_j)^\\top B_j^{-1}(z-\\mu_j)-d\\}$."
      },
      {
        "line": 2750,
        "text": "These expressions differentiate the density at fixed $z$. They do not"
      },
      {
        "line": 2751,
        "text": "differentiate a sampled point along its generating path. For example, draw"
      },
      {
        "line": 2752,
        "text": "$A\\sim\\operatorname{Categorical}(\\pi)$ independently of"
      },
      {
        "line": 2753,
        "text": "$\\varepsilon\\sim\\mathcal N(0,I)$ and set"
      },
      {
        "line": 2754,
        "text": "$Z=\\mu_A+\\operatorname{chol}(B_A)\\varepsilon$. Reusing $\\varepsilon$ in"
      },
      {
        "line": 2755,
        "text": "LEDH initialization preserves both marginal laws and may produce useful"
      },
      {
        "line": 2756,
        "text": "covariance. Averaging several such controls retains the zero center."
      },
      {
        "line": 2757,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 2758,
        "text": "The coupling matters. If instead $G$ is measurable with respect to a cloud"
      },
      {
        "line": 2759,
        "text": "$\\mathcal F$ and additional KDM sampling satisfies"
      },
      {
        "line": 2760,
        "text": "$\\mathbb E[C\\mid\\mathcal F]=0$, then"
      },
      {
        "line": 2761,
        "text": "$\\mathbb E[(G-\\mathbb EG)C^\\top]"
      },
      {
        "line": 2762,
        "text": "=\\mathbb E[(G-\\mathbb EG)\\mathbb E(C^\\top\\mid\\mathcal F)]=0$."
      },
      {
        "line": 2763,
        "text": "Adding independent conditional mixture noise cannot reduce the variance of"
      },
      {
        "line": 2764,
        "text": "that already-computed cloud score through a fixed linear control. Shared"
      },
      {
        "line": 2765,
        "text": "estimating randomness, a correct center, and independent coefficient fitting"
      },
      {
        "line": 2766,
        "text": "are therefore separate requirements. Even when the resulting covariance is"
      },
      {
        "line": 2767,
        "text": "useful, Proposition~\\ref{prop:kdm-density-control} preserves the baseline's"
      },
      {
        "line": 2768,
        "text": "bias relative to the model score."
      },
      {
        "line": 2769,
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "line": 2770,
        "text": "The earlier residual decomposition is still an exact algebraic identity:"
      },
      {
        "line": 2771,
        "text": "\\begin{equation}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2772,
        "text": " L_0^N=A_h+\\left(L_0^N-A_h\\right),\\qquad"
      },
      {
        "line": 2773,
        "text": " \\dd L_0^N=\\dd A_h+\\dd\\left(L_0^N-A_h\\right)."
      },
      {
        "line": 2774,
        "text": " \\label{eq:residual}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2775,
        "text": "\\end{equation}"
      },
      {
        "line": 2776,
        "text": "Dropping the residual changes the target. Computing both terms exactly,"
      },
      {
        "line": 2777,
        "text": "however, gives the original calculation back and supplies no automatic"
      }
    ],
